course: dictionary
lesson: 7236
title: Pi: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word pi can mean a special number or a letter of the Greek alphabet. Look at the words around it to decide.
explain: «The mathematician worked out the value of pi very accurately.» Here pi is a number, because maths words like value and mathematician are the clues. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Capital letters can also give you a clue. «The Raspberry Pi is a cheap, credit-card-sized computer» uses Pi as a name for a small computer. Its clues are computer and coding, not circles.
fact: Pi is a special number, about 3.14, that links the distance around a circle to the distance across it.
fact: Pi can be written as 22/7 or with the symbol π.
fact: The digits of pi go on forever and never repeat.
fact: Pi (π) is also a letter of the Greek alphabet.
fact: Context clues: circles and value show the maths meaning, while computer and coding show the Raspberry Pi.
exercise: «The distance around a circle divided by the distance across it gives pi.» What kind of word is pi here? | A type of shape | *A special number | A Greek letter used in spelling | A kind of computer
exercise: In «The Raspberry Pi is a cheap, credit-card-sized computer made in the UK», what is Pi? | A Greek letter | A special number | A kind of circle | *A small computer made in the UK
exercise: In «The mathematician and astronomer Aryabhata explained that the Earth spins and worked out the value of pi», copy the word that points to maths. | *mathematician | Earth | spins | years
test: What is pi in maths? | A shape with four sides | A type of computer | A Greek letter only | *A special number, about 3.14, linking a circle's distance around and across
test: Pi's digits go on forever. What does this mean? | *Its digits never end and never repeat | It is always a whole number | It repeats every ten digits | The number stops at 3
exam: In «The Raspberry Pi is a cheap, credit-card-sized computer», which word is the best clue that Pi means a computer? | credit-card-sized | UK | *computer | cheap
